-.. Note::
-   Adding rows requires making a new copy of the entire
-   table each time, so in the case of large tables this may be slow.
-   On the other hand, adding columns is fast.
-
-::
-
-  >>> t = Table()
-  >>> t['a'] = [1, 4]
-  >>> t['b'] = [2.0, 5.0]
-  >>> t['c'] = ['x', 'y']
